WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.549 --> 00:00:05.230
These days, it can seem like Hollywood's got
so many sequels on the slate, it's practically

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.000
impossible to keep track of them all.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.860
Never fear, though, here are a few of the
upcoming sequels, prequels and spin-offs that

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.860
might have slipped under your radar.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.920
Many fans thought the day would never come,
but it looks like Ridley Scott is finally

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:24.589
making a sequel to the story of Maximus Decimus
Meridius, nearly 20 years after the original

00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:25.920
Gladiator hit theaters.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.359
Of course, ol' Maximus is busy walking through
wheat fields in heaven, so what's the sequel

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.940
actually going to be about?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.820
According to producer Walter F. Parkes, the
film is going to begin about 20 to 30 years

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.240
after the original ended.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.980
And according to The Hollywood Reporter, part
two will focus on Lucius, the son of Maximus'

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.280
old flame, Lucilla.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.740
While Spencer Treat Clark played Lucius in
the first film, we don't know if he's going

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.080
to reprise his role for Gladiator 2.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.060
What we do know is that Peter Craig is writing
the screenplay, and he's a guy with some pretty

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.730
impressive credits to his name, including
The Town, both Mockingjay movies, and the

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.300
upcoming Top Gun sequel.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:09.340
And with Scott himself behind the camera,
you can be sure it'll be nothing if not entertaining.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:14.970
Based on the comic book series by Mark Millar
and Dave Gibbons, the Kingsman films have

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:20.110
followed the adventures of Gary "Eggsy" Unwin,
a London street thug who joins an organization

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.480
of gentlemen spies.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:28.860
"Manners maketh man."

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.940
Soon enough, he finds himself in a hyper-violent
world of electric lassos and bulletproof umbrellas,

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.060
and now, director Matthew Vaughn wants to
expand on the franchise's quirky and messed-up

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.900
mythology, by finding out how Kingsman came
about in the first place.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:48.780
The King's Man will explain the origins of
the well-dressed intelligence agency, going

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.360
all the way back to the early 20th century.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.680
According to Collider, the story will focus
on an Eggsy-style hero named Conrad, played

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.800
by Harris Dickinson, who gets involved in
World War I.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:05.020
While the exact plot details aren't entirely
certain, the film boasts an impressive lineup

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:12.420
of actors, including Ralph Fiennes, Gemma
Arterton, Charles Dance, Rhys Ifans, Tom Hollander

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.800
and Djimon Hounsou.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.450
Collider also reports that this movie will
feel more like a "period drama than a spy

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.440
thriller," which might make for an interesting
departure from the previous two Kingsman films.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.880
Whatever Matthew Vaughn has in store will
become clear on Valentine's Day, 2020.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.450
Ever wonder what happened to Django and Broomhilda
after they blew Candieland to kingdom come

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.740
in Django Unchained?

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.680
Well, wonder no more, because it looks like
the fastest gun in the South is riding back

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.520
into theaters.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:45.120
According to Collider, Quentin Tarantino is
working on a sequel to Django Unchained, and

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.040
this time, he's teaming up with one of the
most legendary heroes in vigilante history.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.560
Based on a comic series co-written by Tarantino
and Matt Wagner, the sequel will find Django

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.320
forced to escape westwards after burning down
Calvin Candie's plantation.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.200
And that's when he runs into a Spanish nobleman
named Diego de la Vega…who you might know

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.540
better as Zorro.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.460
That's right, Django is reportedly going to
team up with the famous masked swordsman,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.940
and together, these two are going to use bullets
and blades to free the local indigenous people

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.800
from some very nasty bad guys.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.540
That might sound like an incredible premise
for a sequel, but it's not entirely certain

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.500
just how involved Tarantino is going to be
with the whole thing.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.569
He's ultimately in charge of the project,
but the folks at Collider believe he'll be

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:30.480
producing instead of directing.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:35.640
As for the screenplay, comedian Jerrod Carmichael
will be writing the script, but it's also

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.270
uncertain whether Tarantino is co-writing
with Carmichael or simply overseeing the screenplay's

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:40.760
development.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:48.520
One of the most influential shows in TV history,
The Sopranos, came to an end in 2007, not

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.480
with a bang but with a fade to black.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.760
The gangster series earned massive acclaim
throughout its run, set the stage for shows

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:01.400
like Mad Men and Breaking Bad, and gave us
one of television's most iconic characters:

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.320
Tony Soprano.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.850
Now, over a decade later, the show's creator,
David Chase, is bringing his Mafia saga to

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:13.640
the big screen with The Many Saints of Newark,
a movie that serves as a prequel to the Emmy-winning

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.140
series.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:20.400
According to Deadline, the film will be set
in the 1960s, during the deadly Newark riots,

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:26.009
and will focus on Dickie Moltisanti, Tony
Soprano's mentor and Christopher Moltisanti's

00:04:26.009 --> 00:04:26.500
father.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:33.760
The film will also star the likes of Vera
Farmiga, Jon Bernthal, Billy Magnussen, Corey

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.760
Stoll, and Leslie Odom Jr.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.340
And, oh yeah, gangster legend Ray Liotta is
also set to show up.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.460
The screenplay will be co-written by Chase,
and acclaimed TV director Alan Taylor will

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.040
be sitting in the director's chair.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:52.680
In addition to working on Thor: The Dark World
and Game of Thrones, Taylor also directed

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:57.540
several episodes of The Sopranos, which should
make him a natural fit for the prequel.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.479
Speaking with Deadline, Chase explained this
new film will take place in an era when the

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.420
mob was a bit more dapper than they are today.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.180
He said:

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.360
"It is going to depict when it was good.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.979
The mafia was very polished at that time,
how they dressed and what they did…These

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.320
weren't guys who wore tracksuits back then."

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:23.080
But that's not all: a young Tony Soprano is
also going to appear, played by none other

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.060
than Michael Gandolfini, son of James.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:30.629
The Many Saints of Newark is set for release
on September 25th, 2020.

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:37.030
While he'd already won plenty of attention
with movies like Boy and Eagle vs. Shark,

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:41.259
director Taika Waititi really broke into the
cinematic consciousness with his supernatural

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.520
mockumentary What We Do in the Shadows.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:48.840
Starring Waititi himself and fellow New Zealander
Jemaine Clement, this improv-heavy comedy

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:53.560
tells the story of three vampire roommates
just trying to get by in the 21st century.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:58.860
The film wound up on multiple "best of the
year" lists, and since then, Waititi has gone

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:03.420
on to direct a certain little indie picture
you might just have heard of: Thor: Ragnarok.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:08.180
But despite his new role in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, Waititi is still eyeing a return

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.320
to the world of the undead.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:15.280
In January 2016, Waititi told Crave Online
that his Shadows sequel will focus on the

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.120
werewolf pack led by actor Rhys Darby.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.060
"Don't swear.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.080
We’re Werewolves not Swearwolves.”

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.980
“That’s a very offensive word to call
people."

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:32.000
In June, the director explained the plot of
We're Wolves would focus on a power struggle

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.400
between Darby's alpha male and Stu Rutherford's
recently transformed computer programmer.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.000
However, Waititi has explained that making
We're Wolves is going to take a while.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.920
Speaking with IGN, the director said:

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:50.200
"The Jemaine and Taika works is a very long
and slow machine…We put an idea in one end,

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.160
and it takes about six years to come out the
other end.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.040
And sometimes it doesn't even come out."

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:00.249
In other words, We're Wolves is still currently
creeping its way through the creative "sausage

00:07:00.249 --> 00:07:04.719
maker," but if you need your Shadows fix sooner
than later, you'd do well to check out the

00:07:04.719 --> 00:07:10.749
spin-off shows set in the same universe: Wellington
Paranormal and FX's What We Do in the Shadows

00:07:10.749 --> 00:07:11.240
series.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.920
Die Hard could well be the greatest action
movie of the '80s.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.660
In fact, it's probably one of the best action
flicks ever made, full stop.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:24.660
But let's be honest: the series has suffered
in recent years, with the last film bombing

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.659
with critics and tanking at the domestic box
office.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:33.279
So fingers crossed that Die Hard 6, a.k.a.
McClane, can bring a bit of fun back to the

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:33.980
franchise.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:39.080
According to Len Wiseman, who directed Live
Free or Die Hard, the new film will jump back

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:42.200
and forth in time, similar to The Godfather
Part II.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:47.700
In one timeline, we'll have Bruce Willis squaring
off against a team of dastardly terrorists.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:52.920
In another, there'll be a younger John McClane
patrolling the streets of 1970s New York.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:57.520
As for the cast, there's no word yet on who
will play the younger McClane, but Wiseman

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:02.369
has promised the appearance of a young Holly
Gennero, who fans know grows up to become

00:08:02.369 --> 00:08:03.300
McClane's wife.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:07.080
However, there's been a snag in getting the
film to the big screen.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:13.020
Die Hard was originally owned by 20th Century
Fox, but now that Fox has been bought out

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:17.040
by Disney, the folks at the House of Mouse
have to give the movie the go-ahead.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:23.060
Luckily, according to McClane producer Lorenzo
di Bonaventura, Disney does indeed like the

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.780
script, so at the moment, it looks like Die
Hard 6 is still in play.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:32.520
Master and Commander: The Far Side of the
World is one of those movies everybody loves

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.000
today, but nobody saw when it was in theaters.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:40.220
Starring Russell Crowe as a British sea captain
and Paul Bettany as his scientific best bud,

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:44.840
the film follows the adventures of the HMS
Surprise during the Napoleonic Wars.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:49.840
Despite rave reviews, the movie's poor box
office performance seemingly sank the chance

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.520
of a sequel.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:55.750
However, in November 2017, Russell Crowe took
to Twitter and posted this cryptic tweet:

00:08:56.060 --> 00:09:01.360
"For the Aubrey Maturin lovers, I do hear
whispers indeed that a second voyage is perhaps

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.770
potentially pre-proposed a possibility."

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:09.440
Admittedly, it's not a lot to go on, but if
Crowe is on board for such a massive undertaking,

00:09:09.449 --> 00:09:14.820
maybe we'll get to see the further adventures
of Captain Jack Aubrey and Dr. Stephen Maturin

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:15.380
before long.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:20.700
Of course, as Bettany pointed out in May 2018,
Crowe has a history of teasing this sequel

00:09:20.709 --> 00:09:24.690
in hopes of interesting the people with the
pocketbooks, and there's still no telling

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:27.480
whether there's enough studio interest to
get this project going.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:28.700
But if it does?

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:29.920
As Bettany put it:

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.620
"I would revisit those waters in a heartbeat."

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:39.550
Based on the novel by Andre Aciman, Call Me
By Your Name picked up several Oscar nods

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:44.579
at the 90th Academy Awards and even won the
prize for Best Adapted Screenplay, making

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.720
James Ivory the oldest Oscar winner of all
time.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:53.580
The movie made its way onto multiple best-of-the-year
lists, and inspired by its success, director

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.280
Luca Guadagnino has decided he might return
to helm a follow-up.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.751
At the BFI London Film Festival, the Italian
filmmaker said that he wanted to do a sequel

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.920
that takes place several years in the future.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:09.820
It would be set during an era where Timothée
Chalamet's character Elio would be dealing

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.280
with the impact of the Gulf War, the fall
of the Soviet Union, and the rise of the AIDS

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:14.780
epidemic.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.860
He also told The Hollywood Reporter that he
wanted Elio to "be a cinephile," and the sequel

00:10:19.861 --> 00:10:24.970
might open with our protagonist sitting in
a theater, watching Once More, the first French

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.160
film to grapple with the subject of AIDS.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:33.230
Guadagnino is also considering an entire series
of films that follow Elio and his lover Oliver

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.340
as they grow older.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:39.800
Right now, this is all very theoretical, but
Guadagnino is reportedly "serious" about pursuing

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:44.860
a sequel, and Armie Hammer has confirmed that
both he and Chalamet would be up for returning.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.740
"Andre Aciman wants to write another book.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:47.920
Luca wants to write another script.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.400
Timmy and I are down as long as they give
us twelve million dollars."

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:57.700
However, not everyone will be returning if
the film gets going, as the first film's now-Oscar-winning

00:10:57.709 --> 00:11:01.450
screenwriter James Ivory has said he has no
interest in working on a sequel.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:06.199
André Aciman, on the other hand, seems pretty
gung-ho about the whole idea, as he's writing

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.160
a sequel of his own.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:12.480
Will the potential movie take any inspiration
from Aciman's new book, or will Guadagnino

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.180
do his own thing?

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.200
Right now, that remains a mystery.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.500
Do you feel the need?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.800
The need for...a sequel?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:24.980
If not, you'd better get yourself right back
into the danger zone, because Pete "Maverick"

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.340
Mitchell is soaring back into theaters next
year.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:32.760
Over 30 years after Top Gun turned Tom Cruise
into a legitimate star, the A-list actor is

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.600
finally returning for part two.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.460
And he's not the only original cast member
making a comeback.

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:43.860
According to The Wrap, Val Kilmer is set to
return as Tom "Iceman" Kazansky.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.580
But don't expect Top Gun: Maverick to be a
clone of the first film.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:52.540
While nobody knows the plot for sure, Variety
says that Cruise's character will be a flight

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:58.080
instructor, and that the movie will, quote,
"explore a world of drone technology, fifth-generation

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:01.520
fighters, and the end of the era of dog-fighting."

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:06.350
And to represent this brand new world, Miles
Teller is playing the son of Maverick's late-and-great

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.780
wingman, Nick "Goose" Bradshaw, played in
the original by Anthony Edwards.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:14.520
Jennifer Connelly, Jon Hamm, and Ed Harris
will round out the cast.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:19.260
Joseph Kosinski, who previously worked with
Cruise on Oblivion and broke onto the scene

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.580
with Tron: Legacy, is taking the director's
chair.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.900
Expect Top Gun: Maverick to take off on June
26th, 2020.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.699
Widely considered one of the scariest movies
ever made, The Shining certainly seems like

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.480
a clear-cut standalone story.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.600
Jack Torrance dies, and Danny Torrance escapes
the Overlook Hotel.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:39.170
What more needs to be said?

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.140
But there was one person who disagreed with
conventional wisdom and thought The Shining

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.200
needed a sequel.

00:12:44.529 --> 00:12:48.940
Over 35 years after publishing the original
novel, Stephen King returned to the psychic

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.360
world of Danny Torrance with Doctor Sleep.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.820
Published in 2013, the plot follows a middle-aged
Danny as he overcomes alcoholism and uses

00:12:56.820 --> 00:13:00.220
his "shining" abilities to help hospice patients
find peace.

00:13:00.589 --> 00:13:04.620
But things get a little bit complicated after
he befriends a young girl with incredible

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:09.700
powers, as she's being hunted by a cult that
wants to feed off her psychic energy.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:14.420
Following the success of It, Warner Brothers
is adapting Doctor Sleep for the big screen,

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:17.140
and there are some impressive stars joining
the cast.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:22.540
Ewan McGregor will play the older Danny Torrance
and Rebecca Ferguson of Mission: Impossible

00:13:22.551 --> 00:13:28.120
- Rogue Nation is co-starring as the villain
known as Rose the Hat, while Westworld vet

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:32.060
Zahn McClarnon is on board to play her lover
and lieutenant, Crow Daddy.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:38.250
Newcomer Kyleigh Curran will play Abra Stone,
the girl with a psychic gift, and we're also

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.380
going to see the return of some classic Shining
characters.

00:13:42.029 --> 00:13:46.779
Alex Essoe of Starry Eyes will play Danny's
mother, Wendy Torrance, and Carl Lumbly will

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.120
play the telepathic Dick Halloran.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:58.240
"I think a lot of things happened in this particular hotel over the years and not all
of them was good."

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:02.320
So how exactly will Doctor Sleep connect to
the Stanley Kubrick original?

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:07.029
Well, speaking with Bloody Disgusting, director
Mike Flanagan said that while this movie isn't

00:14:07.029 --> 00:14:11.640
The Shining, his sequel will indeed acknowledge
the 1980 horror classic.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:15.020
Doctor Sleep will be released November 8th,
2019.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.520
Ready for some totally bodacious news?

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:23.360
Bill S. Preston and Theodore Logan are re-teaming
for another timey-wimey adventure.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:28.360
Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music takes place nearly
30 years after the duo's Bogus Journey, and

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.940
finds the two excellent rock stars stuck in
a serious mid-life crisis.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:37.100
After a visitor from the future shows up with
a dire warning, Bill and Ted must travel through

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:41.360
time and write a musical masterpiece that
will save all of space-time.

00:14:41.889 --> 00:14:45.880
Along the way, the duo will be joined by their
daughters, played by Brigette Lundy-Pain,

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:50.840
who'll play Ted's daughter, Billie, and Samara
Weaving, who plays Bill's daughter, Thea.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:56.000
Rapper Kid Cudi is also going to show up,
although we don't know who he's going to play,

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.680
while William Sadler is reprising his role
of Death.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:04.680
Dean Parisot of Galaxy Quest fame will direct,
while original screenwriters Chris Matheson

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:09.800
and Ed Solomon will pen the screenplay, and
the legendary Steven Soderbergh will produce.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.470
Even though a whole lot of time has passed
since the last film, screenwriter Ed Solomon

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:19.410
told Collider that part three will "maintain
the tone, the sweetness, the absurdity" of

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.480
the first two while being "something unique."

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:26.780
Prepare to witness Bill and Ted's bogus and
incredible new adventure on August 21st, 2020.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:33.360
In May 2015, The Hollywood Reporter announced
that Sony was set to remake The Craft, the

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.120
black magic cult classic from 1996.

00:15:36.589 --> 00:15:40.399
But as it turns out, that initial report wasn't
100 percent accurate.

00:15:40.399 --> 00:15:44.949
Instead, the filmmakers are taking the Jurassic
World approach, setting the film in the same

00:15:44.949 --> 00:15:50.180
universe but 20 years after the first film,
making it something of a quasi-sequel.

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.320
Producer Douglas Wick told HitFix:

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.520
"There will be callbacks to the original movie,
so you will see there is a connection between

00:15:56.529 --> 00:16:00.519
what happened in the days of The Craft, and
how these [new characters] come across this

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.900
magic many years later."

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:07.140
Leigh Janiak of Honeymoon, who also co-wrote
the original draft of the screenplay, will

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:07.640
direct.

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:13.360
As for actresses, we don't know yet who's
joining the high school coven, but Robin Tunney

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.660
has expressed interest in returning for part
two.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:20.120
Here's hoping the rest of the original cast
will bring back some of the old magic by showing

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.519
up in supporting roles.

00:16:22.529 --> 00:16:28.250
The trippy Jim Henson fantasy Labyrinth is
beloved by a seriously diehard cult following,

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:32.900
and David Bowie's performance as Jareth the
Goblin King has gone down in Hollywood legend.

00:16:33.449 --> 00:16:38.640
So making a sequel to Henson's final film
is bound to be a pretty intimidating task…but

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.220
Fede Alvarez is up to the challenge.

00:16:41.529 --> 00:16:47.140
Luckily, since Alvarez is best known for directing
Don't Breathe and the 2013 Evil Dead remake,

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:50.700
he should have no problem recreating the eerie
atmosphere of the original.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:55.920
At the moment, there aren't any plot details,
other than the film will be "a direct continuation

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:58.980
of the first movie many years later," according
to Alvarez.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:04.060
But rest assured, Labyrinth fans, there won't
be another actor filling in for Bowie.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:08.920
It's impossible for anyone to replace Ziggy
Stardust, after all, so Jareth the Goblin

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.800
King will simply not appear in the upcoming
sequel.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:16.960
And sure, the idea of someone tampering with
such a beloved movie is kind of frightening,

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:19.640
but Alvarez is approaching this film as a
true fan.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.280
As he explained to Deadline:

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:26.120
"Labyrinth is one of the seminal movies from
my childhood that made me fall in love with

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:26.720
filmmaking."

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:31.520
At the moment, it certainly looks like we're
in good hands, although fans probably shouldn't

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.460
hold their breath for the sequel's arrival.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:37.400
Henson Company chairman Brian Henson told
Forbes in 2018:

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.440
"We're still excited about the idea.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:43.910
We are working on something but nothing that's
close enough to say it's about to be in pre-production

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:44.980
or anything like that."

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.300
"It's further than you think."

